hierarchy_code,channel,year,week_num,expected_sales_units,oo_placed
# OPTIONAL FILE. Rename to forecast.csv to activate. One row per
# SKU x channel x ABSOLUTE-YEAR x fiscal-week.
#
# Use this to hand the tool YOUR plan for the FUTURE (unactualised) weeks instead
# of letting it guess (reforecast off last year, or the parametric curve):
#   - expected_sales_units → the initial landing forecast for that week
#                            (replaces the engine guess). Leave BLANK to keep the
#                            engine forecast for that one cell.
#   - oo_placed            → orders you plan to place that week. They land as
#                            receipts at week + lead_time (exactly like typing a
#                            number into the OO Placed column on the grid). Blank/0
#                            = no order; the planner can still add orders on top.
#
# `year` is the real calendar year (NOT a relative TY/LY/LLY label), same keying
# as sales_history.csv. Only UNACTUALISED weeks are honored — real actuals always
# win, so a row for a week that has already closed is ignored.
#
# Any cell you omit falls back to the engine forecast, so the file can be partial:
# cover only the SKUs / weeks you want to pin.
#
# Example (SKU 60001, Ecom): pin wk32 demand at 110 with a 200-unit order, and
# wk33 demand at 120 (no order):
60001,Ecom,2026,32,110,200
60001,Ecom,2026,33,120,0
60001,Ecom,2027,32,121,0
